{"name":"Hot Cocoa","hex":"#806257","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot cocoa","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of hot chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot_cocoa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Hot chocolate, also known as hot cocoa or drinking chocolate, is a heated drink consisting of shaved or melted chocolate or cocoa powder, and heated milk or water. It usually contains a sweetener, such as sugar, and is often garnished with whipped cream or marshmallows. Hot chocolate made with melted chocolate is characterized by less sweetness and a thicker consistency."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/After_The_St._Patrick%27s_Parade_Late_Lunch_%40_Lemon%2C_Dawson_Street%2C_Dublin%2C_Rep._Of_Ireland_A_Fine_Tradition%21_%286992614913%29.jpg/330px-After_The_St._Patrick%27s_Parade_Late_Lunch_%40_Lemon%2C_Dawson_Street%2C_Dublin%2C_Rep._Of_Ireland_A_Fine_Tradition%21_%286992614913%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_chocolate","wikidata":"Q13261"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Chocolatepot.jpg/250px-Chocolatepot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/Chocolatepot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Chocolatepot.jpg/250px-Chocolatepot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silver chocolate pot, France, 1779.[8] Victoria and Albert Museum, London.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocolatepot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Chocolate_cup_Chantilly_porcelain_18th_century.jpg/250px-Chocolate_cup_Chantilly_porcelain_18th_ce